// expect-error: type.array_payload_unsupported
// An array of arrays has no element representation: each element would own
// storage of its own, and an array element is copied and compared in place.
// Ownership inside a container needs a place path down to the element before
// it can be tracked at all.
//
// The rule that refuses this is the parser's admissibility table (ADR 0063):
// `TyPos::ArrayElement` does not admit the array shape. The checker gate
// `check::array_payload_ty` carries the same diagnostic name, because
// `TyPos::gate_name()` maps the position to it, so this fence cannot tell the
// two apart; `array_element_record.sable` is the subject that reaches the
// checker gate.

fn nested() -> u64 {
    [[u64]] rows = alloc_array<[u64]>(1, 0);
    return 0;
}
